# kendex-guard-dialect: legacy-glob
# size-ratchet exclusion list — pattern<TAB>reason, glob against the full
# repo-relative path, `*` crosses `/`. See .agents/skills/size-ratchet/README.md.
#
# Divergence from the fleet's 400/800 split. The engine's 800-line test class
# is a set of path patterns — `tests/*`, `test/*`, `__tests__/*`, `tests.rs`,
# `*test_util.rs`, `*.test.*`, `*.spec.*` — and none of them reach VGS's test
# naming. Go puts `_test.go` beside the source. The script harnesses are
# `scripts/test-*` across .js, .sh and .py alike (test-validate.sh,
# test-section-pointers.py, test-qml-smoke.sh), and the in-tree unit checks are
# `*_selftest.py` and `*-selftest.js` under scripts/lib. Every one of those
# takes the 400-line default and enters the baseline instead — acceptable,
# since a baselined test still cannot grow, and it needs no second gate.
#
# THE THREE VENDOR-DRIFT BASELINE ROWS ARE GONE, with their files: the
# consumer-side vendor-drift checks re-vetted kendex package content, which the
# owner ruled out on 2026-08-26. Their history is in the git log, not here.
# What the sequence taught survives and still applies to the rows below: a
# single 400-line cap repeatedly obstructed correctness work on one small
# cluster of files, and every reviewer finding on them arrived as a size
# argument before it could be fixed. A suite grows by the process's own
# mechanism, one more case per finding, so a cap on a suite taxes coverage; the
# fleet's 800-line test allowance would cover that, and the engine's test class
# does not reach this repo's test naming, as the header above records.
#
# SIX MORE ACCOMMODATIONS, taken by one branch (VGS-150, 2026-08-16), recorded
# here so the paragraph above reads against the real arithmetic rather than
# against three. Measured against origin/main, which is what a reader diffing
# this branch sees; the rows churned more than this within it.
