#
# THE LAST TWO RAISES bought the blockquote. A reviewer found that the repair
# for "a wrapped pointer must keep its target" had been made twice and been
# wrong twice — too broad, then too narrow — and that the shape which motivated
# the finding was still failing: a wrapped quote repeats its `>`, so the target
# line and the mark line read as two structures and the pointer resolved
# against the citing file instead. The fix is small; what it cost is one PAIRED
# control per structural kind, continued-and-joined beside sibling-and-separate,
# because a control on one kind is exactly what let this be wrong twice. Those
# pairs and the paired link/bare-path control are the 43 lines, and the second
# row is their durable record — nine mutants, each run red once.
#
# The granted rows were each raised again by the last review rounds, which
# is the mechanism rather than an exception to it: each round found another
# fail-open, and closing one costs a fix plus the paired controls that pin it.
# Two late raises are worth naming because they are the shape this header
# argues about: one measured a category the guard had been dropping silently
# (8,509 tracked symlinks), and one replaced a file anchor with a directory
# anchor asserted at three depths, because naming a file in a tree the repo is
# about to consolidate made this guard block that consolidation. Both are
# correctness landing as lines.
#
# The two raises are the stronger act, by this header's own distinction, and
# they are not growth of the thing being built: they are the WIRING. Each
# control script costs two manifest rows in scripts/validate and one step in
# ci.yml. That is this branch's contribution to the paragraph above, from a
# direction it had not seen — past a certain size, splitting a file to satisfy
# the cap grows the files that wire the splits together, so the cap stops
# rewarding the split it asked for.
#
# KEN-938 ADDS ONE EXCLUSION AND SEVEN RAISES, in the same shape. The exclusion
# is `.coderabbit.yaml`, which reached 400 of a 400-line threshold: its skill
# lists grow by one line per skill UPSTREAM ships, which this repo does not
# author and cannot decline, and `scripts/check-owned-skills.py` now makes the
# missing line a CI failure — so the next `kendex refresh` that adds a skill
# would fail twice, once for the missing exclusion and once for the line that
# fixes it, with the printed remedy (split at a concept seam) unavailable to a
# single-file bot config a vendor's schema owns. That is the `.agents/*`
# carve-out one file over: a line count tracking upstream inventory rather than
# authored complexity.
#
# THE RAISES, derived from `git diff origin/main...HEAD --
# tools/size-ratchet-baseline.tsv` rather than retyped from an earlier note.
# (`kendex.toml` moves in that diff too, 1082 -> 1078, downward, so it is not a
# raise and is not listed.)
#
#   RAISED    .github/workflows/ci.yml                457 ->  471
#   RAISED    scripts/validate                       1056 -> 1061
#   RAISED    kendex.settings.toml                    425 ->  431
#   RAISED    scripts/check-doc-growth.py             895 ->  955
#   RAISED    scripts/check-section-pointers.py       563 ->  601
#   RAISED    scripts/test-section-pointers.py        458 ->  489
#   RAISED    scripts/test-section-pointers-e2e.py    434 ->  496
#
# THE FIRST TWO ARE WIRING, this header's named cost of a control script paid
# again: one CI step and one manifest row each for the owned-skill register
# guard `scripts/check-owned-skills.py` and its process-level control suite
# `scripts/test-owned-skills-e2e.py`. kendex.settings.toml is the move landing
# in a setting — REVIEW_GATE_CARRY_FORWARD_EXCLUDE swaps `project-skills/*` for
# `.agents/*`, and this repo requires a rationale beside every entry there.
#
# check-doc-growth.py is the `.agents/*` row below reading back on the move.
# That row excludes the skills this repo now owns along with the render it was
# written for, and this list takes no negation, so narrowing it means naming the
# rendered skills by hand — the kind of list KEN-938 removed. Byte ceilings
# cover them instead: three reference files that came out of project-skills/
# with no size gate at all got one, and the owned roots' glob widened from each
# tree's SKILL.md to every file under it, so the next file added to one — a
# reference, a script, a template — is discovered and demands a ceiling of its
# own. No seam divides those entries from the table they are entries in.
#
# THE LAST THREE SHARE ONE REASON. `.agents/` is a SKIP_ROOT, so the move would
# have stopped the pointer sweep reading the skills this repo authors; the guard
# carves them back out by reading the register, and its unreadable-blob arm now
# asks that question through the same predicate instead of spelling it a second
# way. The two suites are those arms' controls, one case per shape, and the e2e
# one pays ten lines a case because every case there is a whole repository.
#
# The three grants are majority code and the growth is five review rounds — 23
# findings, then 12, then 6, then 12 — each asking for another rule, another
# arm, or another reason written down. The `<doc>.md § <section>` pointer guard's
# subsystem is ten files, and every seam anyone has named is already taken:
# three parser libraries (prose_blocks for what counts as prose, pointer_targets
# for which document a token names, section_pointers for where a name ends and
# whether a heading matches), one VCS-access library (tracked_blobs), and five
# control scripts — one per subject, each beside what it pins.
#
# What is left in check-section-pointers.py is one concept that does not divide:
# a check's own policy. Three tables say what it declines to look at
# (HISTORICAL_SECTIONS, FIXTURE_FILES, SKIP_ROOTS) and four say what its result
# must still reach (SWEEP_ANCHORS, TARGET_ANCHORS, ANCHOR_ROOTS,
# GRAMMAR_SPELLINGS); the four collection points assert them, and the run turns
# those into a verdict. Splitting policy from the
# check that applies it would put the tables a reader needs in a second file.
# section_pointers_selftest.py and test-section-pointers-e2e.py are suites, and
# the argument above for a suite applies unchanged: they grow by one case per
# finding, which is the process working. The e2e one is where that is sharpest —
# every case in it is a whole throwaway repository, so a finding costs ten lines
# there rather than two.
#
